//! GCC (Google Congestion Control) sender-side bandwidth estimator.
//!
//! Reads TWCC feedback packets generated by the remote [`TwccReceiverInterceptor`] and
//! estimates available send bandwidth using a trendline delay filter and AIMD rate
//! controller, following draft-ietf-rmcat-gcc-02
//! (Holmer et al., "A Google Congestion Control Algorithm for Real-Time Communication").
//! (RFC 8698 is NADA, a different algorithm, and is not what this implements.)
//!
//! # Chain position
//!
//! GCC must sit **nearer the wire** than [`TwccSenderInterceptor`] so that `handle_write`
//! sees packets after the TWCC sequence number has already been stamped. Put it in
//! [`Slot::CongestionControl`](crate::Slot::CongestionControl), below
//! [`Slot::TwccSender`](crate::Slot::TwccSender):
//!
//! ```text
//! Registry::new()
//!     .with(Slot::CongestionControl, PassThroughInterceptor::new().with(gcc_builder.build()))
//!     .with(Slot::TwccSender, TwccSenderBuilder::new().build())
//! ```
//!
//! Writes walk away from the application toward the wire: TwccSender stamps first, then
//! GCC reads it. TWCC feedback reads reach GCC first, on their way to the application.
//!
//! GCC is a nested interceptor, so it needs an inner end: use
//! [`PassThroughInterceptor`](crate::PassThroughInterceptor), never
//! [`NoopInterceptor`](crate::NoopInterceptor). The latter is the chain's RTCP terminus; wrapped
//! in this slot, the first one inbound packets reach, it would end every RTCP packet nothing
//! marked (NACKs, receiver reports, PLI and FIR) before any other interceptor or the application
//! saw it.
//!
//! # Usage
//!
//! ```ignore
//! use rtc_interceptor::{
//!     GccInterceptorBuilder, Interceptor, PassThroughInterceptor, Registry, Slot,
//!     TwccSenderBuilder,
//! };
//!
//! let (gcc_builder, gcc_handle) = GccInterceptorBuilder::new();
//! let chain = Registry::new()
//!     .with(Slot::CongestionControl, PassThroughInterceptor::new().with(gcc_builder.build()))
//!     .with(Slot::TwccSender, TwccSenderBuilder::new().build())
//!     .build();
//!
//! // In the application polling loop:
//! if let Some(bps) = gcc_handle.target_bitrate_bps() {
//!     encoder.set_bitrate(bps);
//! }
//! ```
//!
//! [`TwccSenderInterceptor`]: crate::TwccSenderInterceptor
//! [`TwccReceiverInterceptor`]: crate::TwccReceiverInterceptor

